## 10. Boundaries — what is NOT built (honest limits)
  - ORCHESTRATOR: 61% of naming information is not in the corpus in any form a counter reaches. structure explains 5.1% of the choice, arguments explain 64.2%, and the residual 2.033 bits is where meaning lives.  [not derivable — a boundary, not a task]
  - VISUAL LANGUAGE FAMILY: 4.7% of the Wikipedia list has no text form: Scratch, Simulink, Max, Grasshopper, Prograph, NXT-G, App Inventor. a language whose source is a picture has no I to collapse.  [indexed so the factory REFUSES rather than guesses]
  - SCALE BEYOND ~17k PARAMETERS: every result here is at 17k params on one primary corpus. a 17M-parameter model may learn an exact stack, in which case the division of labour changes.  [untested — the largest open question]
  - L6 / L7 AS PLANES: 73 and 17 nodes. statistically indistinguishable from L4 at p=0.92 and p=0.94.  [deleted in v2, absorbed into L4]

## 11. Measured-dead — 16 things tried and killed (the real rigor)
  - SWITCHBOARD :: routing (kind, #calls, #args) -> name -> 0.0% top-1 on real held-out functions. the aggregate 20.5% was carried by slots whose answer is 'self'.
  - 8 NAMED ATTENTION HEADS :: prev-token, sink, same-char, class, delimiter, similarity, bigram, uniform -> UNIFORM AVERAGING BEATS THEM: 0.9182 bits vs 0.9256. five of eight already had near-maximal entropy; the two that were sharp duplicated the one-hot features.
  - SEEDED CORPUS GENERATOR :: 600k synthetic tokens from a seed corpus -> the pretraining gain was regularisation in disguise. once L2 and dropout were added it helped nothing.
  - WORD-BIGRAM FILTER :: reject synthetic text with implausible adjacent pairs -> +0.71 accuracy, noise level. the model already had that signal as an input feature.
  - LONG-RANGE COHERENCE GATE :: JS divergence threshold on synthetic text -> 76% rejection for +0.2 perplexity and -0.14 accuracy. failed both metrics.
  - CONSTRAINED SAMPLING :: bias -I fills toward the block centroid -> both intrinsic statistics improved; downstream accuracy fell 0.67%.
  - CORPUS BLENDING :: 94k mixed-register words -> lost to 29k pure by 17 perplexity units. register purity beats volume.
  - CLOSED-FORM READOUT :: ridge solve instead of trained cross-entropy -> 0.86s, zero training, 73.8% top-1 — and 5.082 bits. unusable when sampled: no calibration, no sampling, diversity 1.000 on the generation test.
  - GREEDY DECODING :: argmax instead of sampling -> 5-gram diversity 0.013. one 420-character line, never a newline.
  - WIDER WINDOW :: CTX 26 and CTX 52 -> 52 is WORSE than 13 (49.8% vs 52.9% on brackets). the window was never the bottleneck for prediction.
  - PATTERN IDEMPOTENCE :: forbid a repeated k-statement block -> would forbid 37.33% of real Python. real code repeats a 2-block a third of the time.
  - RUN-LENGTH HARD CAP :: refuse a kind past N repeats -> best cap improves KS by 42% and still differs. kills a genuine 0.23% tail to fix a 4.10% one. replaced by run PRESSURE a=0.3, which agrees at D=0.0099.
  - DENSITY METRIC :: z-distance of construct densities from real code -> shuffled characters scored 0.749 against real code's 0.996. distance-from-average rewards being suspiciously average.
  - BURSTINESS METRIC :: within-sample density variation -> AUC 0.33-0.43 — every condition including noise looked more real than real code.
  - 'CLEAN' AS A QUALITY METRIC :: zero mismatched, zero unclosed -> 20/20 on pure noise. it measured the substrate, never the model. every 30/30 quoted across nine languages was a claim about the veto.
  - GENERIC REGISTER SPILL :: evaluate into R-1 and park in memory -> unfixable in principle: reloading every spilled value into one register loses all but the last. deleted, not repaired. the calling convention handles arity; nothing needs more than 8 registers for depth.

